    "text": "An electric bulb of power&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mn>&nbsp;W</mn></math>&nbsp;has an efficiency of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;and it can be assumed to behave like a point source of light. At a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;from the bulb, the peak value of the electric field in the light produced by the bulb is [Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"
